Azahar opens the joysticks that are already connected before its SDL poll thread starts.

InitJoystick holds joystick_map_mutex while it calls into SDL (SDLJoystick's constructor asks
SDL_GameControllerGetBindForButton, which takes SDL's joystick lock). The poll thread holds SDL's
joystick lock inside SDL_PumpEvents while SDL runs SDLEventWatcher, which waits for
joystick_map_mutex. Upstream starts the poll thread first, so one joystick event during the first
InitJoystick loop deadlocked Azahar before its window opened (observed on the Steam Deck: main
thread in SDL_LockJoysticks under GMainWindow::InitializeWidgets, 0% CPU, no window). Hot-plugged
devices are still opened from the watcher, on the poll thread, where SDL's lock is re-entrant.

--- a/src/input_common/sdl/sdl_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/input_common/sdl/sdl_impl.cpp
@@ -811,6 +811,15 @@
 #endif
 
     SDL_AddEventWatch(&SDLEventWatcher, this);
+
+    // Because the events for joystick connection happens before we have our event watcher
+    // added, we can just open all the joysticks right here. Semu: before the poll thread starts.
+    // InitJoystick holds joystick_map_mutex while it calls into SDL, and the poll thread holds
+    // SDL's joystick lock in SDL_PumpEvents while SDLEventWatcher waits for joystick_map_mutex:
+    // one joystick event during this loop deadlocked Azahar before its window opened.
+    for (int i = 0; i < SDL_NumJoysticks(); ++i) {
+        InitJoystick(i);
+    }
 
     initialized = true;
     if (start_thread) {
@@ -821,11 +830,6 @@
                 std::this_thread::sleep_for(10ms);
             }
         });
-    }
-    // Because the events for joystick connection happens before we have our event watcher
-    // added, we can just open all the joysticks right here
-    for (int i = 0; i < SDL_NumJoysticks(); ++i) {
-        InitJoystick(i);
